Likutay Halachos &mdash; Choshen Mishpat II

Hilchos Shomer Sachar

&sect;16

And this is what is said regarding Aisav, who is the aspect of Amalek, the aspect of the root of the wisdom of nature (Ovadyah 1:5): &ldquo;If thieves came to you,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; &ldquo;How are you made silent,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; &ldquo;How are the things of Aisav searched out, his hidden things laid bare!&rdquo;

For in the future, the forehead of the serpent will be subdued and the forehead of the Ratzon will be revealed. And then the heresies of the sages of nature, who are the aspect of Aisav, will be nullified entirely. And this is: &ldquo;If thieves came to you,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; that is, they will no longer come with the sages of nature through theft. For now they sometimes come through theft and deceptions, as above &mdash; and one must conduct oneself against them also through theft, to incline the da&rsquo;as to emunas haratzon, to steal the souls that were ensnared by them in the net of their error, to incline them to the truth. For now it is impossible to go out against them with an upraised hand, because the forehead of the serpent has not yet been subdued at its root entirely.

But in the future, when the forehead of the serpent will be completely subdued and the root of the Ratzon will be revealed &mdash; then it will be fulfilled: &ldquo;How are the things of Aisav searched out, his hidden things laid bare!&rdquo; For all the hidden things of his wickedness and his heresy will be revealed. For they will be able to subdue him openly, with an upraised hand &mdash; for emunas haratzon will be revealed to the eyes of all.

And then it will be fulfilled: &ldquo;And saviors shall ascend upon Mount Tzion, to judge the mount of Aisav; and the kingship shall be Hashem&rsquo;s&rdquo; (Ovadyah 1:21). For everyone will accept the yoke of His kingship, blessed be He, in love. For it will be revealed to all who come into the world that everything is according to His will, blessed be He, alone &mdash; for Hashem is G&ndash;d, there is nothing else besides Him. Blessed be Hashem forever. Amain v&rsquo;amain.

